 "notes": "Wolf et al. verify the analyzed EOS specimen as (Mg0.87Fe0.13)SiO3 and constrain ferric iron to less than 3% of total Fe; the record therefore represents the ferrous 13% Fe composition, not the existing 12% Fe perovskite material. The article reports Pbnm bridgmanite diffraction and Z=4 unit-cell volumes but no positional refinement for this specimen. For diffraction readiness only, the lattice is the near-composition (Mg0.88Fe0.12)SiO3 ambient cell reported by Knittle and Jeanloz (1987), and the positional scaffold is the Yagi et al. (1978) MgSiO3 Pbnm refinement with 0.87/0.13 Mg/Fe occupancy on the A site. These proxies are not used by the EOS and are not presented as exact refinements of the Wolf specimen.",
